# Where this project finds the Atomcraft TestHarness.
#
#   cp harness.conf.example harness.conf   and edit.
#
# harness.conf is gitignored. The environment wins over it, so a one-off run can set either
# value inline instead. run-tests.sh also reads the harness's own per-user config at
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/atomcraft-test/config, so putting these lines there configures every project
# that consumes the harness at once.
#
# There is no default for either. A checkout lives wherever its owner put it, and a path guessed
# from a sibling directory name goes stale silently the first time that directory is renamed.
#
# Point neither of these at a tree you are developing the harness in. This project does not
# build the harness and does not read its sources, on purpose: a mid-edit checkout does not
# compile, and when that happened it failed this project's tests for reasons that had nothing
# to do with this project.

# The tooling that provisions and launches a patched copy of the game: run-tests.sh,
# bootstrap.sh and lib/. Extract a release source archive from
# https://github.com/sparr/atomcraft-mod-TestHarness/releases, or park a checkout on a release
# tag. Nothing here compiles it.
ATOMCRAFT_HARNESS=""

# A pinned TestHarness.zip from the same release. It supplies both the assembly these mods
# compile against and the harness mod the game loads, so the two cannot disagree. Keep it in
# step with the Harness.RequireVersion pin in test/ModEntry.cs and conformance/ModEntry.cs --
# a mismatch is reported by the harness at load time as a refused mod.
ATOMCRAFT_HARNESS_ZIP=""
